---
import { mastheadStamp } from "../dossiers/headline.js";
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import EveryCut from './EveryCut.astro';
import GuideData from './GuideData.astro';
import {bySlug,kicker} from '../dossiers/registry.js';
import {pensionsModel} from '../dossiers/pensions.model.js';
import {pensionFormat} from '../dossiers/pensions.format.js';
import {governedPensionPayload,governedPensionPayloadText} from '../dossiers/pensions.payload.js';
interface Props { model?: any; entry?: any }
const D=Astro.props.entry??bySlug.pensions,model=Astro.props.model??pensionsModel();
if(!D||D.sourceQualityMode!=='required')throw Error('Governed pension guide registry is required');
const inputs=model.manifest.bundles.map(b=>b.slug).join(', '),h=model.headline,F=model.readerFacts;
const groups=[...new Set(model.plates.map(p=>p.group))];
const payload=governedPensionPayload(model.plates),sourceURL='https://www.pfrda.org.in/en/research-publications/statistics/statistical-data';
// Reader formats for the prose: Indian scale words, never more digits than the sentence needs.
const MONTHS={Jan:'January',Feb:'February',Mar:'March',Apr:'April',May:'May',Jun:'June',Jul:'July',Aug:'August',Sep:'September',Oct:'October',Nov:'November',Dec:'December'};
const when=p=>p.replace(/^([A-Z][a-z]{2}) (\d{4})$/,(_,m,y)=>`${MONTHS[m]} ${y}`);
const say=f=>f.unit==='inr_crore'?(f.value>=1e5?`₹${(f.value/1e5).toFixed(2)} lakh crore`:`₹${Math.round(f.value).toLocaleString('en-IN')} crore`):f.value>=1e7?`${(f.value/1e7).toFixed(2)} crore`:f.value>=1e5?`${(f.value/1e5).toFixed(1)} lakh`:Math.round(f.value).toLocaleString('en-IN');
const n=(id)=>({id:'n-'+id,text:say(F[id])});
---
<Base title="Pensions and retirement saving · India Atlas" description={D.description} nav="guides" dateStamp={mastheadStamp(D)} crumbLeft='<a href="/guides/">Guides</a> / Households / <b>Pensions</b>' crumbRight={`${D.statusNote}, <b>${D.version}</b>`} canonical="https://atlas.thisindianlife.today/guides/pensions/" ogImage="/og/pensions.png">
<div class="page pensions-guide">
 <div class="titleblock break" data-inputs={h.bundle} data-prose="evergreen and source-bound facts">
  <div class="kicker">{kicker(D)}</div><div class="hero-grid"><h1 set:html={D.headline}/><p class="lede">Most Indians who work will never draw a government or company pension. Two schemes run by the pension regulator, the National Pension System and Atal Pension Yojana, are how a growing number of them now save for old age. This guide follows who has joined, how much money the schemes hold, and what people do when they take it out.</p></div>
  <div class="meta"><span>Latest month <b>{when(h.lastSourcePeriod)}</b></span><span>Source <b>Pension Fund Regulatory and Development Authority (PFRDA)</b></span><span>Measure <b>Accounts and money at the end of each period</b></span></div>
  <div class="numbers"><div class="num"><div class="l">Atal Pension Yojana subscribers</div><div class="v acc" id="n-pensions-apy" data-source-bundle={h.bundle} data-source-key={h.key}>{pensionFormat(h.lastSourceValue,h.unit)}</div><div class="d">Accounts at the end of {when(h.lastSourcePeriod)}</div></div><div class="num"><div class="l">State government employees in the NPS</div><div class="v" id={n('sg_members').id}>{n('sg_members').text}</div><div class="d">The largest group within the NPS</div></div><div class="num"><div class="l">Money held for state government employees</div><div class="v" id={n('sg_aum').id}>{n('sg_aum').text}</div><div class="d">Assets under management, {when(F.sg_aum.period)}</div></div></div>
 </div>
 <section data-inputs={h.bundle} data-prose="evergreen"><div class="sec-head"><h2>Saving for the years after work</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="reading-cols"><div class="reading-col"><p>A government clerk who joined service before 2004 retires on a pension the state pays for life. Her colleague who joined in 2010 does not: he has an NPS account, into which he and the government pay each month, and his income after 60 depends on what that account has grown to. A shopkeeper or a farm worker has neither, unless they choose to save.</p><p>The National Pension System began in 2004 for new central government employees. Most states followed, then employers in the private sector, and since 2009 anyone can open an account on their own.</p></div><div class="reading-col"><p>Atal Pension Yojana, launched in 2015, is built for low earners outside formal jobs. A member pays a small fixed amount each month until 60 and is promised a fixed monthly pension after that, with the government making up any shortfall.</p><p>An account is a start, not a retirement income. Many accounts receive small or irregular payments, and the money a member ends up with depends on how long and how much they paid in.</p></div></div></section>
 <section data-inputs={inputs} data-prose="methodology"><div class="sec-head"><h2>How to read these figures</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="wm-grid"><div><p><b>Accounts, not people.</b> The figures count accounts at the end of each month or year. One person can hold more than one, for example an NPS account and an APY account, and an account counts whether or not money still goes into it.</p><p><b>Assets move with markets.</b> Assets under management are the value of the money invested on the members' behalf. They rise with new contributions and with returns on shares and bonds, and fall when markets fall or money is withdrawn.</p><p><b>Each chart is one series as PFRDA publishes it.</b> Monthly charts run to the latest month published; yearly charts follow the financial year, April to March. The categories overlap in places, so the series are not added together here.</p><p><b>Expected is not actual.</b> The retirement chart shows PFRDA's estimate of how many subscribers will reach retirement age in coming years. It is drawn with a dashed line and hollow dots.</p></div><div class="wm-rail"><aside class="margin-note"><span class="mk">Coverage</span>These schemes are a part of India's retirement saving. Provident funds, old-style government pensions and private savings are outside them.</aside><aside class="margin-note"><span class="mk">Revisions</span>PFRDA does not publish when it revises a table. <span id="prov-vintage">Source revision date: not published.</span></aside></div></div></section>
 <section id="current-reading" data-inputs={inputs} data-prose="source-bound facts"><div class="sec-head"><h2>What the figures show</h2><span class="line"></span><span class="unit">{when(h.lastSourcePeriod)}</span></div><div class="reading-cols"><div class="reading-col"><p>Atal Pension Yojana has grown into the largest scheme by far. Within the NPS, state government employees are the biggest group, at <b id={n('sg_members').id+'-r'}>{n('sg_members').text}</b> accounts, ahead of individuals who joined on their own (<b id={n('all_citizen_members').id}>{n('all_citizen_members').text}</b>), employees in company schemes (<b id={n('corporate_members').id}>{n('corporate_members').text}</b>) and central government staff (<b id={n('cg_members').id}>{n('cg_members').text}</b>). <b id={n('employers').id}>{n('employers').text}</b> employers offered the NPS by {F.employers.period}.</p><p>NPS Lite, the older scheme for informal workers, peaked at <b id={n('lite_peak').id}>{n('lite_peak').text}</b> accounts in {when(F.lite_peak.period)} and has since fallen to <b id={n('lite_members').id}>{n('lite_members').text}</b>.</p></div><div class="reading-col"><p>The money is concentrated where the salaries are. State government employees' accounts hold <b id={n('sg_aum').id+'-r'}>{n('sg_aum').text}</b> and central government accounts <b id={n('cg_aum').id}>{n('cg_aum').text}</b>. APY, with many times their members, holds <b id={n('apy_aum').id}>{n('apy_aum').text}</b>, because its members pay in small amounts.</p><p>In {F.withdrawals_processed.period}, PFRDA processed <b id={n('withdrawals_processed').id}>{n('withdrawals_processed').text}</b> requests to withdraw part of the savings early, <b id={n('housing_withdrawals').id}>{n('housing_withdrawals').text}</b> of them to buy or build a house. <b id={n('annuities').id}>{n('annuities').text}</b> people bought an annuity at retirement or exit that year.</p></div></div></section>
 {groups.map(group=><section data-inputs={[...new Set(model.plates.filter(p=>p.group===group).map(p=>p.bundle))].join(', ')} data-prose="evergreen explanations and source-bound values"><div class="sec-head"><h2>{group}</h2><span class="line"></span></div>{model.plates.filter(p=>p.group===group).map(p=><div class="break"><figure id={'cb-'+p.id} data-inputs={p.bundle} data-series-key={p.lines[0].key} data-observation-kind={p.sourceQuality.observationKind}><div class="plate-head"><div class="t"><h3>{p.title}</h3><div class="sub">{p.observationKind==='expected-schedule'?'Expected. ':''}{p.unit==='inr_crore'?'₹ crore':'Accounts'}, to {when(p.period)}.</div></div><div class="plate-val"><div class="v" id={'pv-'+p.id}>{pensionFormat(p.rows[0].value,p.unit)}</div><div class="c">{p.observationKind==='expected-schedule'?'Expected, '+p.period:when(p.period)}</div></div></div><div class="frame"><div class="plotzone" id={'plot-'+p.id}></div><div class="plotfoot"><span class="src">Source: PFRDA, table {p.sourceId}, {p.sourceTitle.toLowerCase()}.</span><div class="dl"><button data-dl="svg">SVG</button><button data-dl="png">PNG</button><button data-dl="csv">CSV</button><a href={p.sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source ↗</a></div></div></div><div class="explain"><div class="ev"><span class="mk">How to read this</span><p>{p.explain}</p></div></div></figure></div>)}</section>)}
 <section data-inputs={inputs} data-prose="evergreen"><div class="sec-head"><h2>Common misreadings</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="reading-cols"><div class="reading-col"><p><b>"Crores of Indians now have a pension."</b> They have an account. Whether it pays a living income at 60 depends on years of regular contributions, and many accounts get little.</p><p><b>"The fund with the most money performs best."</b> A fund manager's assets reflect which schemes and members it was given, not its returns.</p></div><div class="reading-col"><p><b>"These are all of India's pensions."</b> Provident funds, the old government pension, and private savings and insurance sit outside these figures.</p><p><b>"Expected retirements are people who have retired."</b> The retirement chart is PFRDA's estimate of who reaches retirement age, not exits that have happened or pensions paid.</p></div></div></section>
 <EveryCut slug="pensions"/><GuideData slug="pensions"/>
 <section data-inputs={inputs} data-prose="methodology"><div class="sec-head"><h2>Sources</h2><span class="line"></span></div><p>Every figure comes from the statistical tables PFRDA publishes on its website, monthly for subscribers and assets and yearly for the rest. The charts above answer one question each; every other series, including assets by pension fund and scheme, enrolments by age and sex, and grievances, is in the table above and the downloads. Some PFRDA tables are not yet charted or included because their units or definitions need checking against the publisher. <a href={sourceURL}>PFRDA statistical data</a>.</p></section>
</div>
<script is:inline type="application/json" id="pensions-data" set:html={governedPensionPayloadText(payload)}/>
<script>import '../dossiers/pensions.client.js';import '../dossiers/guide.client.js';</script>
</Base>
<style is:global>
 .pensions-guide .plotzone>svg[data-compact="pensions"]{min-width:0;max-width:100%;height:auto}
 .pensions-guide .plate-val .v{font-size:clamp(1.2rem,2.7vw,1.8rem)}
</style>
